body:
When trying to run a browser build on a Windows PC it’s not possible to proceed because a popup appears that redirects the user to the File Manager Plus app in the Android Play Store. This behavior prevents using the browser build outside of Android.

The issue seems to be caused by the following code block:

```
if (window.location.hostname !== '127.0.0.1' && window.location.hostname !== 'localhost') {
  var msg = (i18nStrings && i18nStrings[lang] && i18nStrings[lang].fileManagerAlert);
  alert(msg);
  window.location.href = 'https://play.google.com/store/apps/details?id=com.alphainventor.filemanager';
}

```
Steps to Reproduce:

Run a browser build of AAPS on a Windows PC

- open it in a local browser

- observe the popup and redirection

If this redirect is intentional, please update the documentation accordingly:

https://androidaps.readthedocs.io/en/latest/SettingUpAaps/BrowserBuild.html
